vlc: raise chain-filter recursion limit (CHAIN_LEVEL_MAX 2 -> 5)

The chroma chain helper (modules/video_chroma/chain.c) bails out with
"Too high level of recursion (N)" when constructing chains that need
more than CHAIN_LEVEL_MAX+1 (= 3) filter levels in series. This bites
users who combine two pixel-reading filters (e.g. postproc +
autoupscale) with hardware decode, because VLC must thread a hw->sw
download converter between the decoder and the first filter, pushing
the chain to 4 deep:

    HW_decoder -> hw->sw_converter -> postproc -> autoupscale -> vout
                                          (already 3 levels into recursion)

Bumping CHAIN_LEVEL_MAX from 2 to 5 lets these chains construct
without any filter or syntax changes from the user's side. Higher
values risk longer chain-search times in pathological cases but the
search is bounded by the available filter modules; 5 is conservative.

NB: the constant is named CHAIN_LEVEL_MAX (not MAX_CHAIN_LEVEL) and
lives in modules/video_chroma/chain.c (not src/misc/filter_chain.c).
The error is triggered by `level > CHAIN_LEVEL_MAX`, so the limit
fires one above the constant's value (default 2 -> error at 3).

Apply with:

    cd /path/to/vlc-source        # tag 3.0.20 verified
    patch -p1 < /path/to/this/file.patch

Then rebuild VLC normally.

This patch is unaffiliated with VideoLAN; it's offered as a workaround
for a specific deep-chain scenario, not a recommended upstream change.
If you find it useful, consider sending it upstream with a clear
reproducer.

---

diff --git a/modules/video_chroma/chain.c b/modules/video_chroma/chain.c
--- a/modules/video_chroma/chain.c
+++ b/modules/video_chroma/chain.c
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@ static picture_t *BufferChainedFilters( filter_t *p_filter )
     return filter_NewPicture( p_parent );
 }

-#define CHAIN_LEVEL_MAX 2
+#define CHAIN_LEVEL_MAX 5

 /*****************************************************************************
  * Activate: allocate a chroma function
